WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:19.951
Izzie hurried into the gym with her beach bucket.

2
00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:23.771
It was her first day back at camp after vacation.

3
00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:27.445
"Should we hide these?" she asked Mr. Dunn.

4
00:00:27.446 --> 00:00:29.989
"Before everyone else gets here?"

5
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.013
He looked into the bucket of seashells.

6
00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:36.445
"Yep. Let's go!"

7
00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:39.773
Izzie and Mr. Dunn went out to the playground.

8
00:00:39.774 --> 00:00:44.494
They hid Izzie's shells under the swings and behind the soccer goals.

9
00:00:44.495 --> 00:00:48.616
They hid more shells around the basketball nets and trees.

10
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:52.862
They finished just as the other campers arrived.

11
00:00:52.863 --> 00:00:57.438
On the blacktop Mr. Dunn explained the day's activity.

12
00:00:57.439 --> 00:01:01.374
"Today you'll hunt for secret treasures.

13
00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:04.161
I can't tell you what they are."

14
00:01:04.162 --> 00:01:08.351
"Then how are we supposed to find them?" Bobby asked.

15
00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:13.172
Mr. Dunn grinned. "I'll give you a clue.

16
00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.467
The treasures are from the sea.

17
00:01:16.468 --> 00:01:20.613
When you've found five items, bring them to the table."

18
00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:23.073
"Yeah," Izzie added.

19
00:01:23.074 --> 00:01:25.780
"We're going to make something cool!"

20
00:01:25.781 --> 00:01:34.713
"Good luck!" Mr. Dunn waved the hunters off.

21
00:01:34.714 --> 00:01:39.637
"That clue wasn't very helpful," Jason complained.

22
00:01:39.638 --> 00:01:41.831
"Yes it was.

23
00:01:41.832 --> 00:01:45.415
I know what we're hunting for," Bobby bragged.

24
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:48.380
"I figured it out!"

25
00:01:48.381 --> 00:01:53.319
Just then Nina shouted, "I found something!"

26
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.916
The boys ran to Nina, who was by the swings.

27
00:01:56.917 --> 00:02:02.707
"Watch where you step!" she squealed. "They're delicate!"

28
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.638
"What are?" Jason asked.

29
00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:10.328
Nina opened up her hands. "The seashells."

30
00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:16.099
Once the campers knew what they were looking for, the seashells were easy to find.

31
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.318
Soon they were all at the table.

32
00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:24.156
"We've got our seashells," Ethan said. "Now what?"

33
00:02:24.157 --> 00:02:30.592
"Well," Mr. Dunn said, "Izzie kindly collected these seashells from the beach for us.

34
00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:37.006
And her dad drilled tiny holes in each one.

35
00:02:37.007 --> 00:02:40.173
So I'll let her explain today's craft."

36
00:02:40.174 --> 00:02:42.844
Izzie beamed proudly.

37
00:02:42.845 --> 00:02:46.167
"We're making sea-breeze wind chimes."

38
00:02:46.168 --> 00:02:48.473
She held up a chime.

39
00:02:48.474 --> 00:02:51.254
"My family made this one last year.

40
00:02:51.255 --> 00:02:55.102
It has four shells and one piece of sea glass.

41
00:02:55.103 --> 00:02:58.920
And this is real driftwood."

42
00:02:58.921 --> 00:03:02.459
"What's driftwood?" asked Bobby.

43
00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.657
"Wood that's been floating in the sea for awhile," said Ethan.

44
00:03:06.658 --> 00:03:10.879
"I brought you guys some driftwood too," Izzie added.

45
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.616
"Thanks," Nina said.

46
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:16.034
"How do we make the chimes?"

47
00:03:16.035 --> 00:03:22.088
"It's easy. You just have to tie everything to the wood," Izzie said.

48
00:03:22.089 --> 00:03:24.979
"First we have to make the hanger.

49
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:29.958
Cut a piece of string about sixty centimeters long.

50
00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:33.993
Tie one end of the string around one end of your stick.

51
00:03:33.994 --> 00:03:38.930
Then tie the other end of the string to the other end of the stick.

52
00:03:38.931 --> 00:03:43.790
Now we're ready to attach the shells to the chime.

53
00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:50.797
Cut five pieces of string about thirty centimeters long each.

54
00:03:50.798 --> 00:03:55.264
Thread one string through the hole in one shell and knot it.

55
00:03:55.265 --> 00:03:59.377
Then tie the other end of the string to the driftwood.

56
00:03:59.378 --> 00:04:05.987
Keep doing this until all your shells are hanging down from the wood."

57
00:04:05.988 --> 00:04:10.598
The campers laid out their shells, cut string, and got to work.

58
00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:15.558
"Make sure the knots are tight," Mr. Dunn said.

59
00:04:15.559 --> 00:04:18.886
"Hey, Izzie, thanks," Ethan said.

60
00:04:18.887 --> 00:04:22.330
"This reminds me of the beach in California."

61
00:04:22.331 --> 00:04:24.924
"You're welcome," Izzie said.

62
00:04:24.925 --> 00:04:29.842
She tied a small pink scallop shell to her wind chime and smiled.

63
00:04:29.843 --> 00:04:34.427
Today she shared a fun part of her beach vacation with her friends.

64
00:04:34.428 --> 00:04:41.923
And that felt as cool as a sea breeze!
